{#
  On this page — the note's h2s as a nav of anchors, for a panel beside the
  prose (see .c-content__aside / _toc.scss). Real links, so it works without
  JS; toc.js marks the section in view.

  A <details>, so on a phone — where it sits in the flow above the prose — it
  can fold to its one-line title and be opened on tap. It ships OPEN: without
  JS the list is simply there; toc.js closes it on narrow screens and keeps it
  open on wide ones, where the summary is just the panel's title.

    headings — [{ id, text }] from craft.frontend.headingAnchors
#}
{% if headings is defined and headings|length %}
    <nav class="c-toc" aria-label="Summary" data-toc>
        <details class="c-toc__details" open>
            <summary class="c-toc__whisper u-font-whisper">Summary</summary>
            <ol class="c-toc__items">
                {% for h in headings %}
                    <li class="c-toc__item"><a class="c-toc__link" href="#{{ h.id }}">{{ h.text }}</a></li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ol>
        </details>
    </nav>
{% endif %}
